 @sapphyrus  This is such a brain dead take and is comparable to saying that someone is backwards because they aren't playing any Direct Storage games. Well that's because there aren't any.
Outside of a handful of titles, RT is only good for photomode. The effects, at least the way they're implemented now, are so subtle that you just won't notice during gameplay. This is not going to change any time soon, especially with cards capable of delivering acceptable RT performance being brutally overpriced. Game developers are not going to cater to these cards when the most common GPU on Steam is GTX 1650. And by the time that changes, what we're seeing here suggests that AMD won't be doing that much worse even without dedicated RT hardware. Nvidia should absolutely annihilate AMD's RT performance here, but that's clearly not happening. 

So while RT itself will be awesome some time in the future, dedicated RT hardware may end up going the path of dedicated PhysX hardware. And let's be frank, DLSS is already slowly going that way, FSR is going to dominate because of its wider availability. Remember what happened to Gsync.

